PARITY (web EditConflictBanner.tsx → native)
  Data sources (P1/S8 state-holder seam, no HTTP in the view):
    useEditLease(resourceKey) → EditConflictSource emits EditConflictInput (the lease state — isOwner +
                             otherTab{tabId,claimedAt} — for the controlled resourceKey / resourceLabel,
                             plus the feed's load / connectivity state). The view never reads the lease
                             coordinator directly. claim() → source.claim() (web performClaim).
    useTranslation         → EditConflictStrings P1/S10 facade (every literal keyed).
  Render guard: web `if (isOwner || otherTab === null) return null` → hasConflict = !isOwner && otherTab != nil.
                Web null (no conflict) → native friendly `empty` leaf (never a blank box; P4 leaf contract).
  Composition: warning-toned alert banner (web variant="warning" → statusWarning) + warning icon (web
               <AlertTriangle/>), the title, the reassurance body, and "Take over editing" (ghost, sm,
               → claim) + the muted switch hint (web text-xs text-muted span). ViewThatFits reflows the
               action + hint beneath the body on narrow widths (web `flex-wrap`). Carries resourceKey +
               otherTabID through the payload (web data-resource-key / data-other-tab-id parity).
  Body branch: resourceLabel ? t('editConflict.banner.bodyWithLabel','{{resource}} is open in another tab…')
                             : t('editConflict.banner.body','This resource is open in another tab…');
               empty resourceLabel falls back to the generic key (web truthiness). {{resource}} interpolated.
  Take-over:   web "Take over editing" → claim() → performClaim (isOwner=true, otherTab=null + broadcast).
               Native takeOver(): optimistic owner promotion (banner hides in lockstep) + source.claim()
               + onTakeOver parent hook. A later snapshot still governs, so the banner reappears if a new
               peer wins the lease back (web tiebreaker behaviour) — unit asserted.
  i18n keys (web → catalog, ALL 5 reproduced — no scope narrowing): editConflict.banner.title, .body,
               .bodyWithLabel, .takeOver, .switchHint — all present; + P4 leaf chrome + freshness keys.
  States rendered (every one, no hidden surface): loading, empty (owner OR no-peer), error, data, stale, offline.

